<title>CANADA: TENNIS-RESULTS TUESDAY AT CANADIAN OPEN.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-RESULTS TUESDAY AT CANADIAN OPEN.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results from the $2.3 million</p>
<p>Canadian Open men's tennis tournament on Tuesday (prefix</p>
<p>number denotes seeding):</p>
<p>First round</p>
<p>11-Patrick Rafter (Australia) beat Olivier Delaitre (France)</p>
<p>6-4 6-1</p>
<p>Fabrice Santoro (France) beat 14-Jim Courier (U.S.) 7-5 4-6</p>
<p>6-4</p>
<p>15-Alex O'Brien (U.S.) beat Arnaud Boetsch (France) 6-1 6-2</p>
<p>Sandon Stolle (Australia) beat Sebastien Lareau (Canada) 6-1</p>
<p>7-5</p>
<p>Jeff Salzenstein (U.S.) beat Wade McGuire (U.S.) 6-4 6-2</p>
<p>Michael Tebbutt (Australia) beat Frederic Niemeyer (Canada)</p>
<p>7-6 (7-5) 6-3</p>
<p>Cristiano Caratti (Italy) beat Martin Damm (Czech Republic)</p>
<p>6-3 6-1</p>
<p>Steve Campbell (U.S.) beat Cecil Mamitt (U.S.) 6-1 4-6 7-5</p>
<p>Guillaume Raoux (France) beat Pier Gauthier (France) 6-3 7-6</p>
<p>(7-3)</p>
<p>Brett Steven (New Zealand) beat Frederik Fetterlein (Denmark)</p>
<p>6-2 6-0</p>
<p>Second round</p>
<p>4-Yevgeny Kafelnikov (Russia) beat Vince Spadea (U.S.) 4-6</p>
<p>6-3 7-6 (8-6)</p>
<p>6-Gustavo Kuerten (Brazil) beat Jonathan Stark (U.S.) 6-2 6-4</p>
<p>8-Richard Krajicek (Netherlands) beat Neville Godwin (South</p>
<p>Africa) 7-6 (7-3) 6-1</p>
<p>12-Jonas Bjorkman (Sweden) beat Doug Flach (U.S.) 5-7 6-3 7-5</p>
<p>16-Jan Siemerink (Sweden) beat Chris Woodruff (U.S.) 6-7</p>
<p>(4-7) 7-5 7-6 (7-2)</p>
</text>
